#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702676 :multistep/context "Source: Problem 5(a–c), PDF page 6.\n\n**Stream functions produce streamlines.** Let $\\mathbf F=\\langle f,g\\rangle$ be source-free and let $\\psi$ be its stream function, meaning\n\n$$\\psi_y=f,\\qquad\\psi_x=-g.$$\n\nLet $P=(x,y)$ lie on the level curve $\\psi(x,y)=c$. Think of the level curve locally as $y=y(x)$. The source's dependency diagram shows $\\psi$ depending on both $x$ and $y$, with $y$ itself depending on $x$; thus the composite is $\\psi(x,y(x))$." :multistep/id #uuid "df893de7-f13c-5602-9b56-5e571d7a8b23" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702508 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702521}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702543 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702509}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702669 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702690}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702702 :multistep/context "Source: Problem 2(a–c), each with tasks (i–iv), PDF page 3.\n\nLet $C$ be the counterclockwise unit circle centered at the origin. For each field in parts (a), (b), and (c): (i) find its domain; (ii) calculate the indicated integral by hand; (iii) calculate it “using” Green's theorem; and (iv) compare (ii) and (iii), using (i) to explain any difference." :multistep/id #uuid "ffbba298-c987-52cc-b2d6-0f6398a806ca" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702510 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702496}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702513 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702610}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702544 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702573}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702555 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702582}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702557 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702576}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702565 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702634}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702578 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702482}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702605 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702484}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702625 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702581}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702635 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702645}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702674 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702656}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702695 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186702673}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719435 :multistep/context "Source: Problem 1(a–d), PDF page 2.\n\nFind the requested functions on the field's domain, noting any distinction between a local branch and a globally defined function. **Source hint:** There is a related problem in this week's written homework." :multistep/id #uuid "0922e70e-242a-53d4-aed4-35319a95be31" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719439 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719499}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719488 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719482}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719502 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719501}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719504 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719447}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719438 :multistep/context "Source: Problem 4(a–e), PDF page 5.\n\nSuppose $f(x)$ is differentiable on $[a,b]$. Let\n\n$$R=[a,b]\\times[0,1]=\\{(x,y):a\\le x\\le b,\\ 0\\le y\\le1\\},\\qquad\\mathbf F=\\langle0,f(x)\\rangle.$$\n\nOrient the boundary of $R$ counterclockwise.\n\n![Rectangle R with x-coordinates a and b and height 1](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Frectangle-4.png)" :multistep/id #uuid "0cccca78-5ab8-5f7a-b657-e72e03bb81d8" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719436 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719433}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719444 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719487}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719446 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719496}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719461 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719468}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719481 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719464}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719472 :multistep/context "Source: Problem 2(a–b), PDF page 3." :multistep/id #uuid "8fa50f74-ea14-57c5-9cc7-9684c0dbd2ba" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719454 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719431}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719473 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719457}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719478 :multistep/context "Source: Problem 5(a–b), PDF page 6.\n\nConsider the cardioid\n\n$$\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle\\cos t(1-\\sin t),\\ \\sin t(1-\\sin t)\\rangle,\\qquad0\\le t\\le2\\pi.$$\n\n![Source cardioid r=1-sin(t)](/api/asset?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F255%2FR-5%2Fcardioid-5.png)" :multistep/id #uuid "a317f78d-2e52-59e3-a1f6-c0539bed7e46" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719452 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719497}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719486 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719490}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719500 :multistep/context "Source: Problem 3(a–b), PDF page 4." :multistep/id #uuid "e5b2bfad-c83c-57c1-8b1b-52629c2657a6" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719474 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719442}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719485 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186719498}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725563 :multistep/context "Source question: assignment PDF page 5, parts (a)–(b)." :multistep/id #uuid "24eac539-1d1f-5d3e-9a5b-6548e8a30e27" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725655 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725594}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725743 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725625}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725570 :multistep/context "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 5](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_3/5).\n\nA tank contains 100 kg of salt in 1,000 L of water. A salt solution at 0.05 kg/L enters at 6 L/min. The mixture is well mixed and drains at the same rate." :multistep/id #uuid "2e4a8ff4-b5a4-58ff-aa56-54620f973f94" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725565 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725685}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725598 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725551}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725613 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725680}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725592 :multistep/context "Source question: [WeBWorK Problem 2](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_3/2).\n\nA bacteria culture starts with 340 bacteria and grows at a rate proportional to its size. After 4 hours there are 1,360 bacteria." :multistep/id #uuid "402d7e8e-8b30-53fb-af25-20e73b0b1230" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725559 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725560}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725669 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725623}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725732 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725572}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725600 :multistep/context "Source question: assignment PDF page 2, parts (a)–(d).\n\nFrom 1944 through 1989 Hanford produced 67.4 metric tons of plutonium. The worksheet estimates that 189 kg of plutonium-239 waste was disposed of there; its stated half-life is 24,110 years. Determine how many years after 1989 must pass until 50 kg remains, through the steps below. The worksheet cites [PNNL-21651](https://www.pnnl.gov/main/publications/external/technical_reports/PNNL-21651.pdf) for its historical context. Use the given 189 kg as the initial radioactive-waste mass, not the production total." :multistep/id #uuid "47487696-3bc2-5709-ae88-e6a9369af351" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725603 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725617}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725671 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725586}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725704 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725634}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725737 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725539}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725639 :multistep/context "Source question: assignment PDF page 6, parts (a)–(d); page 7 is workspace.\n\nA tank initially contains 15 pounds of sugar in 120 gallons of water. A solution containing $1/4$ pound of sugar per gallon enters at 8 gal/min, and the well-mixed solution leaves at the same rate." :multistep/id #uuid "7835a1b5-b6f5-5b13-b3ef-c715427fef90" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725553 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725659}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725582 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725629}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725616 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725548}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725670 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725638}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725668 :multistep/context "Source question: assignment PDF page 1, parts (a)–(d).\n\nA petri dish initially contains 2,000 bacteria and contains 20,000 after 10 hours. Assume $P\\prime(t)=rP(t)$, $P(0)=2000$." :multistep/id #uuid "9dc17ff2-9a03-5c98-affa-8baa7d351dfa" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725579 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725608}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725633 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725610}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725686 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725637}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725718 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725665}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725687 :multistep/context "Source question: assignment PDF pages 3–4, parts (a)–(d).\n\nStart with $\\theta\\!\\prime\\!\\prime(t)=-g\\sin\\theta(t)$ for a simple pendulum of length $1\\,m$, with the source’s stated value $g=9.8$. Let $v=d\\theta/dt$." :multistep/id #uuid "b653dfdc-5aa2-5384-b6a9-cdd76f0a543f" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725567 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725591}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725581 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725653}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725660 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725587}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725734 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725730}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725689 :multistep/context "Source question: assignment PDF pages 1–2, parts (a)–(d).\n\nStart with Newton’s equation $mx\\!\\prime\\!\\prime(t)=-kx(t)$ for a mass on a spring, where $m$ and $k$ are constants. Let $v=dx/dt$." :multistep/id #uuid "b7bfb444-59a3-5902-826c-b74f77959f82" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725534 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725724}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725604 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725624}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725701 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725575}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725729 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186725618}}]}]}
